\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Left: the selection funnel. The three denominators the text keeps apart are the catalogued population, the 168-entry ALMA-covered work list, the ${\sim }115$ stars a public field genuinely contains, and the 90{} searched. Right: the experiment in eleven{} steps with the number surviving each, matching \S  \ref  {sec:summary} line for line --- from the public execution blocks in scope, through the pre-registered hold-out and the window inventory, to the candidate tests. The 512-control comparison at step\nobreakspace  {}7 is a candidate-generation screen and not a test of the null; step\nobreakspace  {}8 is the same screen with the radial gradient removed. Every count is read from the generated macros, so the figure, the list and the released catalogue cannot disagree.}}{5}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:funnel}{{3}{5}{Left: the selection funnel. The three denominators the text keeps apart are the catalogued population, the \NCensus -entry ALMA-covered work list, the ${\sim }\NGenuinelyCovered $ stars a public field genuinely contains, and the \NStars {} searched. Right: the experiment in \NFunnelStepsWord {} steps with the number surviving each, matching \S \ref {sec:summary} line for line --- from the public execution blocks in scope, through the pre-registered hold-out and the window inventory, to the candidate tests. The \NCtrl -control comparison at step~7 is a candidate-generation screen and not a test of the null; step~8 is the same screen with the radial gradient removed. Every count is read from the generated macros, so the figure, the list and the released catalogue cannot disagree}{figure.3}{}}
