\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Where this survey searched. \emph  {Lower panel:} each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance and labelled alternately on the left and right axes; heavy blue marks the fine-channel carrier search (Class\nobreakspace  {}A) and light grey the coarse-channel spectral-excess search (Class\nobreakspace  {}B). \emph  {Upper panel:} the number of systems covering each gigahertz of sky frequency. The panel shows coverage and search class only; the threshold distribution is Fig.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {fig:context}. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: 46{} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $24.0\times $ the union. The union is the frequency coverage; the summed bandwidth is the integrated search effort, and the two answer different questions (Scope of the constraints, \S  \ref  {sec:method}).}}{6}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:waterfall}{{4}{6}{Where this survey searched. \emph {Lower panel:} each searched window is a horizontal segment on its host system's row, rows ordered by distance and labelled alternately on the left and right axes; heavy blue marks the fine-channel carrier search (Class~A) and light grey the coarse-channel spectral-excess search (Class~B). \emph {Upper panel:} the number of systems covering each gigahertz of sky frequency. The panel shows coverage and search class only; the threshold distribution is Fig.~\ref {fig:context}. The coverage is narrow, clustered and repeatedly revisited: \UnionIntervals {} islands concentrated near 230 and 345\,GHz, with summed window bandwidth $\GrossOverUnion \times $ the union. The union is the frequency coverage; the summed bandwidth is the integrated search effort, and the two answer different questions (Scope of the constraints, \S \ref {sec:method})}{figure.4}{}}
