\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces \emph  {(a)}\nobreakspace  {}Class\nobreakspace  {}A sensitivity. Cumulative number of independent systems whose best window reaches a given EIRP, for $P_{90}^{\rm  sel}$, the power passing the complete automated selection (solid), and for $P_{90}$, which reaches the trigger only (dashed). The shaded band is the systematic budget: the window-to-window transfer bracket $\times 0.48$--$\times 1.35$, which dominates, together with the one-sided $+20$ per cent atmospheric-decorrelation bias, which can only make the quoted power optimistic. It is asymmetric for that reason. \emph  {(b)}\nobreakspace  {}The temporal selection function: systems grouped by the longest separation between their searched epochs, an independent epoch being defined as a separation of more than 1{} day. \textbf  {For the 27{} systems with a single block and the 13{} whose blocks all fall within one day --- left of the dashed line --- independent confirmation was not possible at all}, whatever the sensitivity in panel\nobreakspace  {}(a). Recurrence over years can be tested for 23{} systems.}}{14}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:classasens}{{7}{14}{\emph {(a)}~Class~A sensitivity. Cumulative number of independent systems whose best window reaches a given EIRP, for $P_{90}^{\rm sel}$, the power passing the complete automated selection (solid), and for $P_{90}$, which reaches the trigger only (dashed). The shaded band is the systematic budget: the window-to-window transfer bracket $\times \StratTransferNineLo $--$\times \StratTransferNineHi $, which dominates, together with the one-sided $+\BudDecorHi $ per cent atmospheric-decorrelation bias, which can only make the quoted power optimistic. It is asymmetric for that reason. \emph {(b)}~The temporal selection function: systems grouped by the longest separation between their searched epochs, an independent epoch being defined as a separation of more than \EpSep {} day. \textbf {For the \EpOne {} systems with a single block and the \EpSameDay {} whose blocks all fall within one day --- left of the dashed line --- independent confirmation was not possible at all}, whatever the sensitivity in panel~(a). Recurrence over years can be tested for \EpYears {} systems}{figure.7}{}}
