\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {17}{\ignorespaces Array-split robustness. The control geometry uses a 12-m $\theta _{\rm  PB}$ for every window, so the ACA 7-m stratum carries a known geometric error. Expected rank-first counts are $N_{\rm  win}/(512+1)$ under exchangeability, and are therefore lower bounds: the measured tail rate is a factor 1.4{} higher (\S  \ref  {sec:empiricalfa}), which brings the 12\,m stratum's 9{} observed within one of expectation. No disposition and no headline threshold depends on the ACA windows.}}{37}{table.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:arraysplit}{{17}{37}{Array-split robustness. The control geometry uses a 12-m $\theta _{\rm PB}$ for every window, so the ACA 7-m stratum carries a known geometric error. Expected rank-first counts are $N_{\rm win}/(\NCtrl +1)$ under exchangeability, and are therefore lower bounds: the measured tail rate is a factor \PseudoFirstRatio {} higher (\S \ref {sec:empiricalfa}), which brings the 12\,m stratum's \NStageOneTwelveM {} observed within one of expectation. No disposition and no headline threshold depends on the ACA windows}{table.17}{}}
