\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces The stage-1 star--band pairs, scored under both statistics, so the difference between them can be audited. The superseded region-maximum statistic flags 66{} windows in 41{} star--band pairs across the survey, far more than the symmetric statistic; this table gives the pairs either statistic promotes to stage\nobreakspace  {}1, not all 66{} of them. $S_{\rm  reg}$: region maximum of Eq.\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {eq:tstar} over $n_{\rm  src}=135$ positions; $T_\star $: the symmetric single-position statistic; `ctrl max', `ring max': the largest control statistic under each. The $\nu $ column is each window's \emph  {centre}; the crossing frequency differs by up to 0.85\,GHz, and Table\nobreakspace  {}\ref  {tab:flagged} carries $\nu _{\rm  cross}$. For CP$-$72\nobreakspace  {}2713 the region maximum already lay on the star, so the two coincide.}}{40}{table.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:bothstats}{{19}{40}{The stage-1 star--band pairs, scored under both statistics, so the difference between them can be audited. The superseded region-maximum statistic flags \NRegionMaxFlag {} windows in \NRegionMaxPairs {} star--band pairs across the survey, far more than the symmetric statistic; this table gives the pairs either statistic promotes to stage~1, not all \NRegionMaxFlag {} of them. $S_{\rm reg}$: region maximum of Eq.~\ref {eq:tstar} over $n_{\rm src}=135$ positions; $T_\star $: the symmetric single-position statistic; `ctrl max', `ring max': the largest control statistic under each. The $\nu $ column is each window's \emph {centre}; the crossing frequency differs by up to 0.85\,GHz, and Table~\ref {tab:flagged} carries $\nu _{\rm cross}$. For CP$-$72~2713 the region maximum already lay on the star, so the two coincide}{table.19}{}}
