\newlabel{tab:repaired}{{20}{40}{The survey rescored under both repairs. ``Survives'' is the largest stellar debit $m(0)$, in units of each window's own control scale, at which the star still exceeds every detrended control; it is a property of the window and assumes neither debit. For reference the conservative debit is \RmDebitCons $\,\sigma $ and the debit that centres the calibration-sample rank distribution is \RmDebitCal $\,\sigma $, and a window survives whichever debit is smaller than its entry. No window is added by either repair}{table.20}{}}
