\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces Visibility-domain test for emission at the stellar position, for all 13{} stage-1 windows. Every visibility in the event's own channel is phase-rotated to the star and averaged: emission centred there gives a positive real part and an imaginary part consistent with zero, while emission displaced from the star is suppressed in the real part and in general leaves a non-zero imaginary part. $N_{\rm  vis}$ is the number of visibilities averaged, $\sigma $ the standard error over them, and `ctrl' the largest real part returned by eight control positions on the annulus of \S  \ref  {sec:statistic}. The events attributed to carbon monoxide are the test's controls: 7{} are recovered at $10$--$59\sigma $, HD\nobreakspace  {}48370 shows the displaced-source signature its foreground identification predicts, and one $\beta $\nobreakspace  {}Pictoris block could only be tested at a substituted frequency. All 13{} execution blocks were recalibrated from the raw archive for this test.}}{42}{table.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:visibility}{{21}{42}{Visibility-domain test for emission at the stellar position, for all \NVisTested {} stage-1 windows. Every visibility in the event's own channel is phase-rotated to the star and averaged: emission centred there gives a positive real part and an imaginary part consistent with zero, while emission displaced from the star is suppressed in the real part and in general leaves a non-zero imaginary part. $N_{\rm vis}$ is the number of visibilities averaged, $\sigma $ the standard error over them, and `ctrl' the largest real part returned by eight control positions on the annulus of \S \ref {sec:statistic}. The events attributed to carbon monoxide are the test's controls: \NVisAttRecov {} are recovered at $\VisAttReLo $--$\VisAttReHi \sigma $, HD~48370 shows the displaced-source signature its foreground identification predicts, and one $\beta $~Pictoris block could only be tested at a substituted frequency. All \NVisTested {} execution blocks were recalibrated from the raw archive for this test}{table.21}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces The CP$-$72\nobreakspace  {}2713 repeat test in full, both blocks side by side, so the reader can tell ``not detected again'' from ``a persistent signal of the original strength would have been recovered''. The repeat block is the deeper of the two, matches the first in tuning, channelisation and integration, and its frequency axis registers to a fifth of a channel. A source at the first block's flux would have returned $T_\star =6.21$ there; the measured value is 4.70. Intermittent emission is not excluded by this test, and no statement here assumes otherwise.}}{42}{table.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:cprepeat}{{22}{42}{The CP$-$72~2713 repeat test in full, both blocks side by side, so the reader can tell ``not detected again'' from ``a persistent signal of the original strength would have been recovered''. The repeat block is the deeper of the two, matches the first in tuning, channelisation and integration, and its frequency axis registers to a fifth of a channel. A source at the first block's flux would have returned $T_\star =\CpRecExpT $ there; the measured value is \CpTstarTwo . Intermittent emission is not excluded by this test, and no statement here assumes otherwise}{table.22}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces The injection campaign resolved by configuration. $P_{50}$ and $P_{90}$ are the injected amplitudes, in units of the local noise, at which half and nine-tenths of trials are recovered. No axis shows a deficit large enough to move the quoted threshold outside the window-to-window bracket of $\times 0.48$--$\times 1.35$; the sub-channel-phase rows are mean response factors, not recovery amplitudes, and are the reason the threshold carries a response correction.}}{42}{table.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:driftstrata}{{23}{42}{The injection campaign resolved by configuration. $P_{50}$ and $P_{90}$ are the injected amplitudes, in units of the local noise, at which half and nine-tenths of trials are recovered. No axis shows a deficit large enough to move the quoted threshold outside the window-to-window bracket of $\times \StratTransferNineLo $--$\times \StratTransferNineHi $; the sub-channel-phase rows are mean response factors, not recovery amplitudes, and are the reason the threshold carries a response correction}{table.23}{}}
